[Music]  the term elastic Cloud growing or  shrinking Cloud resources in a pinch has  become a bit of a buzzword but when then  automatically it can be really powerful  and you can do so automatically on  Google Cloud VMware engine or gcve to  expand or Shrink the cluster in your  private Cloud environment  in this video you will learn about the  auto scaling policies in gcve and how to  configure it to manage Dynamic workloads  much more efficiently  gcp offers different types of Auto scale  policies like storage capacity CPU  performance memory performance and CPU  and memory performance optimization  policies you can choose to apply an  appropriate policy based on your needs  let's start by looking at each of these  policies in more detail  storage capacity optimization policy  adds a node when storage consumption  goes above 80 percent and removes a node  when storage consumption goes below 40  percent  CPU performance optimization policy adds  a node when CPU utilization goes above  70 percent or storage consumption goes  above 80 percent and removes a node when  CPU utilization goes below 45 percent  and storage consumption goes below 40  percent  memory performance optimization policy  adds a note when memory utilization goes  above 80 percent or storage consumption  goes above 80 percent and removes a node  when memory utilization goes below 45  percent and storage consumption goes  below 40 percent  CPU and memory performance optimization  policy adds a node when CPU utilization  goes above 70 percent on memory  utilization goes above 80 percent or  storage consumption goes above 80  percent and removes the node when CPU  utilization goes below 45 percent and  memory utilization goes below 45 percent  and storage consumption goes below 40  percent be aware there are some  scenarios or limitations under which  Auto scaling doesn't work in GCV private  Cloud environments firstly if the GCV  nodes have reached the maximum number of  nodes for the cluster or maximum quota  for the region then Auto scaling cannot  add any more nodes next if the GCB nodes  have reached their minimum limit  configured for the cluster then Auto  scaling will not remove any nodes  lastly Auto scale policies are not  available on clusters containing a  single node  to configure or modify Auto scale policy  in your private Cloud environment you  must have the identity and access  management or IAM role VMware engine  service admin this role has admin access  to VMware engine resources and the  required permissions to perform these  tasks  now let's dive into a demo and configure  storage capacity optimization policy on  a cluster  in the Google Cloud console go to the  VMware engine page from the left pane  click on resources followed by the  private Cloud name where you want to  configure Auto scale  click on the Clusters tab to list the  Clusters within that private Cloud click  on the pencil icon to edit the auto  scale policy configuration of the  specific cluster select the auto scale  policy drop down menu  choose an appropriate Auto scale policy  based on your requirements in this  example we will select storage capacity  optimization policy  in the add nodes drop down you can  specify the number of nodes to be added  by Auto scale remember only one node can  be removed at a time so remove nodes is  grayed out  you can use the slider to set the cool  off period default value is 30 minutes  this means VMware engine will trigger  the auto scale action to add or remove  nodes if the metrics breached the  threshold for the time duration  specified in the cool off period  in the node limits option you can  specify the minimum and maximum count of  nodes which cluster can be shrunk or  expanded to using Auto scale  in our demo we will retain the default  values of 3 and 4 respectively  finally click the submit button  congratulations the cluster has been  configured to Auto scale nodes in this  private cloud  to learn more about Auto scale policies  and configuring it in your private Cloud  environment check out this documentation  thanks for watching foreign

